cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you reference this project or its methodology in academic work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "BloomBelly: An AI-Assisted Arabic-First Maternal and Child Health Platform"
abstract: >
  BloomBelly is a Flutter-based mobile health platform combining AI-driven medical
  image analysis, a fine-tuned conversational agent, and an interpretable nutrition
  classifier to support Arabic-speaking pregnant women, second-time mothers, and
  their partners. The system orchestrates three AI components — Google Gemini for
  medical image interpretation, a LoRA-tuned transformer for clinical Q&A, and a
  Random Forest classifier for stage-appropriate nutrition guidance — behind a
  Python Flask backend with Supabase persistence, served through a Provider-based
  MVVM Flutter client. The work was developed as a graduation thesis at the
  College of Informatics Engineering, Al-Sham Private University, Damascus, Syria.

